# Shared Product Card

## Single Source of Truth

`src/modules/category/components/CategoryProductCard.tsx` is the **only** product card component for all listing pages.

```typescript
import { CategoryProductCard } from '@/modules/category/components/CategoryProductCard';

// Works in home page, category page, profile wishlist — everywhere
<CategoryProductCard item={item} />
```

Accepts `CategoryItem` from `src/modules/category/hooks/useCategoryItems.ts`.

## What It Does Internally

- **Navigation** — clicking the image navigates to `/products/${item.id}`
- **Wishlist** — heart button uses `useWishlist()` (auth-gated, persisted)
- **Badge** — shown if `item.badge` is set (e.g. `'NEW'`, `'Sold Out'`)

## Navigation Pattern (Stretched Link on Image)

Clicking the image (`<Link>` wrapping the image container) navigates to the product detail. The heart button inside uses `e.preventDefault() + e.stopPropagation()` to prevent navigation.

```tsx
<Link href={`/products/${item.id}`} className="relative block ...">
  <Image ... />
  <button onClick={(e) => { e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation(); toggle(item.id); }}>
    ♥
  </button>
</Link>
```

## Rules

- **Never** create a new product card component — extend `CategoryProductCard` instead
- **Never** pass `isFav`/`onToggleFav` as props — wishlist is handled internally
- `CategoryItem` is the normalized type — all data sources must map to it via `useCategoryItems` or `useWishlistItems`
